The Security Council,

Recalling the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations, in particular the sovereign equality of all States, political independence, territorial integrity, non-interference in the internal affairs of States and the obligation of all States to refrain from the threat or use of force in their international relations,

Reaffirming its primary responsibility for the maintenance of international peace and security,

Deeply concerned by the deteriorating humanitarian situation in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela and its impact on the Venezuelan people and neighbouring countries, and by the violence and loss of life that have occurred in recent days, including at the country’s borders,

Reaffirming the sovereignty, political independence, unity and territorial integrity of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela and the right of the Venezuelan people to determine their own future without external interference,

Stressing the need for a peaceful and inclusive political solution to the current situation in Venezuela through dialogue and negotiation among all Venezuelan actors, in accordance with the Constitution and laws of Venezuela,

Emphasizing that humanitarian assistance should be provided in accordance with the principles of humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence and with the relevant provisions of General Assembly resolution 46/182 of 19 December 1991, including the consent and coordination of the affected State,

Noting the regional mediation efforts, including the Montevideo Mechanism, aimed at promoting peaceful dialogue and a solution among Venezuelans,

Expressing concern at actions that could lead to further escalation and instability in Venezuela and the region, and underscoring the need to prevent any escalation,

1. Calls upon all Venezuelan actors to refrain from violence, exercise maximum restraint, ensure the safety and protection of civilians and respect human rights and fundamental freedoms;

2. Reaffirms the sovereignty, political independence, unity and territorial integrity of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela and the principle of non-interference in its internal affairs;

3. Calls upon all States to refrain from the threat or use of force and from any action inconsistent with the Charter of the United Nations, and to avoid actions that could exacerbate tensions or undermine the peaceful settlement of the situation in Venezuela;

4. Encourages all Venezuelan political and social actors to engage, without preconditions and in good faith, in an inclusive and credible political dialogue and negotiation, with full respect for the Constitution and laws of Venezuela, in order to overcome the current crisis and find a peaceful solution;

5. Calls for safe, unhindered and sustained humanitarian access to those in need in Venezuela, in accordance with the humanitarian principles of humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence and in coordination with the relevant Venezuelan authorities, and stresses that humanitarian assistance should not be used for political purposes or as a pretext for intervention;

6. Requests the Secretary-General to use his good offices to support dialogue and humanitarian access, in cooperation with regional organizations, and to keep the Council informed as appropriate;

7. Calls upon all States and regional organizations to support a peaceful, democratic and Venezuelan-led solution to the situation in Venezuela and to refrain from any action that may contribute to further escalation or instability;

8. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

