4. Encourages all Venezuelan political and social actors, including the National Assembly and all other constitutionally established institutions, to engage, without preconditions and in good faith, in an inclusive and credible political dialogue and negotiation, with full respect for the Constitution and laws of Venezuela, in order to overcome the current crisis and find a peaceful solution, including through the holding of free, fair, transparent and credible elections in accordance with the Constitution and laws of Venezuela and with the participation of all political actors;

5. Calls for safe, unhindered and sustained humanitarian access to those in need in Venezuela, including across land borders and lines of conflict and through all available routes, in accordance with the humanitarian principles of humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence and in coordination with the United Nations and impartial humanitarian actors, without prejudice to the consent and coordination of the affected State as appropriate, and stresses that humanitarian assistance should not be used for political purposes, subject to political conditions, or obstructed by any actor;

6. Requests the Secretary-General to use his good offices to support dialogue and humanitarian access, in cooperation with regional organizations, including the International Contact Group and the Montevideo Mechanism, and to keep the Council informed as appropriate;

7. Calls upon all States and regional organizations to support a peaceful, democratic and Venezuelan-led solution to the situation in Venezuela and to refrain from any action that may contribute to further escalation or instability;

8. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

